      "writtenOn": "2023-11-10T20:34:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know much about the DTS format so I may be misreading this but \nin a later CL [fpc1025.h\n](https://crrev.com/c/4866410/31/zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fpc1025.h) defines the following:\n\n```\nstruct fpc1025_cfg {\n\tstruct spi_dt_spec spi;\n\tstruct gpio_dt_spec interrupt;\n\tstruct gpio_dt_spec reset_pin;\n\tstruct fingerprint_info info;\n};\n```\n\nI believe the `struct fingerprint_info info;` is a representation of this DTS config. Then in [fpc1025.c](https://crrev.com/c/4866410/31/zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fpc1025.c) from the same CL the `reset_pin` and `interrupt` signals seem to use the versions from `fpc_1025_cfg` rather than from `fingerprint_info`. Are the GPIO definitions here still needed?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "7f7ee0bf33ad9a8bfe748f8fedce1b2758314ff0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1d4e228_262dc512",
